      "writtenOn": "2026-04-03T13:54:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I also agree the ramoops approach seems much better (although it is not obvious to me how to implement it without substantial changes in the implementation of ramoops itself, to make it aware that a part of the ramoops buffer is the hypervisor buffer and so on).\n\nAs for resetting the system from the hypervisor, hopefully that\u0027s easy: the hypervisor could just write the ACPI reset register (whose address it could get from the FADT table before deprivileging)?\n\n...So I\u0027m probably fine with either BUG_ON or WARN_ON_ONCE here, whatever you guys think is better.",
